---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';

const title = 'About TarkovTools: Who We Are & Why These Tools Exist';
const description =
  'TarkovTools is an independent fan toolset for Escape from Tarkov: ballistics charts, penetration maths, loadout tools. Free and honest.';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', href: '/' },
  { name: 'About' },
];
---

<Base title={title} description={description} breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs} canonical="/about/">
  <div class="wrap-narrow">
    <Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbs} />

    <h1>About TarkovTools</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Ballistics answers for raiders who want numbers, not vibes: exact ammo data, honest penetration
      models, and a planner that tells you what to actually load.
    </p>

    <section class="section">
      <h2 id="why">Why this site exists</h2>
      <p>
        Ammo in Tarkov is a spreadsheet game disguised as a shooter: dozens of rounds across nine
        calibers, penetration values that decide fights before they start, and armor classes that make
        half of your stash useless against the wrong opponent. The data exists (tarkov.dev's API is
        excellent), but turning it into a decision ("what do I bring to this raid") still takes tabs,
        spreadsheets and guesswork.
      </p>
      <p>
        TarkovTools compresses that into three tools: the chart (browse), the calculator (penetration
        vs armor), and the solver (best round for your situation).
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2 id="how">How the tools are built &amp; tested</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Data from tarkov.dev.</strong> Ammo and armor stats come from the community's open tarkov.dev dataset, the same source that powers most modern Tarkov tools; compile notes on the <a href="/methodology/">methodology page</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Documented model, published limits.</strong> Penetration maths follows the community model with its approximations stated openly, no hidden fudge factors.</li>
        <li><strong>Client-side.</strong> No accounts, no uploads, works offline once loaded.</li>
        <li><strong>Corrections welcome.</strong> If a stat is wrong or a patch changed the maths, <a href="/contact/">tell us</a>.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2 id="money">How the site makes money</h2>
      <p>
        Right now: nothing. TarkovTools is independent and self-funded. Any future sponsorships will be
        clearly labelled and never affect data or recommendations.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2 id="people">Who runs it</h2>
      <p>
        A small crew of Tarkov veterans and software engineers. We have been killed by every ammo type
        in this game and have opinions about all of them.
      </p>
      <p class="small muted">
        For corrections: <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> or {site.email}.
      </p>
      <p class="small muted">
        TarkovTools is an unofficial fan project, not affiliated with Battlestate Games.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
